# Context

## Why This Way
The README follows progressive disclosure on purpose: pitch, features,
and quickstart sit above the fold; exhaustive detail (environment table,
the 19-package map) folds into <details> blocks; everything else links
to SPEC.md and deploy/README.md instead of duplicating them.

Choices a future editor should keep:

- The quickstart writes a fresh .env with `cat >` rather than appending
  to a copy of env.example. That avoids relying on Docker Compose
  duplicate-key precedence inside one .env file.
- The development section tells readers to export the environment
  (`set -a; . ./.env; set +a`). Verified: tsx does not auto-load .env,
  and apps read process.env directly. Without that step the dev path
  dead-ends.
- Screenshots come from the e2e fixture server against the production
  build: real UI, synthetic fixture data, no real mail. Regenerate with
  `npm run build --workspace=@mail-hub/web`, `node e2e/fixture-server.mjs`,
  then drive the cached Playwright Chromium at 1280x800, scale 2.
- The status section claims only what DEVICE-MATRIX.md records. Safari
  on macOS and a real iPhone stay listed as unverified.

## Gotchas
- The screenshot images are 2560px wide at 2x scale; keep new captures
  at the same scale so the header layout stays balanced.
